425 - Holy, Holy, Is What the Angels Sing
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 425
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[A]There is singing up [G]in heaven such as we have never known,
[A]Where the angels sing the praises of the Lamb upon the throne;
[A]Their sweet harps are ever [D/A]tuneful and their voices always clear,
[A/E]O that we might be more like them while we [A7/G]serve the Master here!
[A7/G]Holy, holy, is [D/F#]what the angels sing,
[D/F#]And I expect to help them make the courts of heaven ring;
[D/A]But when I sing redemption's story, they will fold their wings,
[D]For angels never felt the joys that our salvation brings.

Refrain:
[D/F#]Holy, holy, is what the angels sing,
[D/A]And I expect to help them make
[D/A]the courts of heaven ring;
[Em/G]But when I sing redemption's story,
[Em/G]they will fold their wings,
[D/F#]For angels never felt the joys
[D/F#]that our salvation brings.

Verse 2:
[A]But I hear [G]another anthem,
[A]blending voices clear and strong,
[A]"Unto Him [D/A]who hath redeemed us
[A/E]and hath bought us," is [A7/G]the song;
[A7/G]We have come thro' [D/F#]tribulations
[D/F#]to this land so fair and bright,
[D/A]In the fountain freely flowing
[D]He hath made our garments white.

Verse 3:
[A]Then the angels [G]stand and listen,
[A]for they cannot join that song,
[A]Like the sound [D/A]of many waters,
[A/E]by that happy, blood-washed [A7/G]throng;
[A7/G]For they sing about [D/F#]great trials,
[D/F#]battles fought and vict'ries won,
[D/A]And they praised the great Redeemer,
[D]who hath said to them, "Well done."

Verse 4:
[A]So, although [G]I'm not an angel,
[A]yet I know that over there
[A]I will join [D/A]a blessed chorus
[A/E]that the angels cannot [A7/G]share;
[A7/G]I will sing about [D/F#]my Savior,
[D/F#]who upon dark Calvary
[D/A]Freely pardoned my transgressions,
[D]died to set the sinner free.
